# lane_split.jsonl - the regression test for suppression rule 2.\n\nA motorcycle at 8 m/s filtering north between two cars at 5 m/s, holding a\nsteady 1.5 m lateral gap to each. Radii 1.0 + 2.0 = 3.0 against a 1.5 m gap,\nso the circle model reports a severe conflict on essentially every frame of\nthe overtake. All of it is completely routine behaviour on an Indian road,\nand a human labeller marks none of it.\n\nEXPECTED OUTPUT: ZERO EVENTS.\n\nRun it with --set suppression.lane_splitting=false and it emits severe\nevents instead. That contrast is the demo beat for rule 2.\n\nIf this file starts producing events with the rule on, the conflict stream\non real footage is about to be flooded with two-wheelers doing nothing\nwrong, and recall against C's labels will collapse.
